1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,040
AI doesn't read text the way we do.

2
00:00:02,180 --> 00:00:04,230
It reads your prompt as tokens: tiny

3
00:00:04,270 --> 00:00:05,850
chunks of words, spaces, and

4
00:00:05,910 --> 00:00:06,610
punctuation.

5
00:00:06,690 --> 00:00:08,490
That's why this sentence doesn't become

6
00:00:08,540 --> 00:00:09,020
one thing.

7
00:00:09,100 --> 00:00:11,060
It gets broken into pieces the model can

8
00:00:11,120 --> 00:00:11,680
process.

9
00:00:11,810 --> 00:00:12,430
Artificial.

10
00:00:12,560 --> 00:00:13,320
Intelligence.

11
00:00:13,390 --> 00:00:13,730
Is.

12
00:00:13,940 --> 00:00:14,360
Wonder.

13
00:00:14,470 --> 00:00:14,810
Ful.

14
00:00:14,920 --> 00:00:15,360
Period.

15
00:00:15,560 --> 00:00:17,550
Even the space before a word can become

16
00:00:17,600 --> 00:00:18,370
part of the token.

17
00:00:18,500 --> 00:00:20,400
A good mental shortcut: one token is

18
00:00:20,460 --> 00:00:22,000
roughly three quarters of an English

19
00:00:22,050 --> 00:00:22,300
word.

20
00:00:22,440 --> 00:00:23,890
Not exact, but close enough for

21
00:00:23,940 --> 00:00:24,340
planning.

22
00:00:24,500 --> 00:00:26,460
Now the important part: tokens are also

23
00:00:26,540 --> 00:00:28,260
how we measure the context window.

24
00:00:28,340 --> 00:00:30,020
The context window is the model's

25
00:00:30,080 --> 00:00:31,030
short-term memory.

26
00:00:31,090 --> 00:00:33,170
It can only see so many tokens at once.

27
00:00:33,260 --> 00:00:35,070
When the window gets too full, older

28
00:00:35,130 --> 00:00:36,350
tokens slide out of view.

29
00:00:36,500 --> 00:00:38,250
That's why very long chats can lose

30
00:00:38,310 --> 00:00:39,180
earlier details.

31
00:00:39,290 --> 00:00:41,010
So when you prompt, think in tokens:

32
00:00:41,160 --> 00:00:42,830
what does the model need to see right

33
00:00:42,890 --> 00:00:43,110
now?

34
